<title>USA: Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn buys Pherrovet.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn buys Pherrovet.</headline>
<dateline>KALAMAZOO, Mich. 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn's Animal Health unit said Thursday it has acquired  Pherrovet Group, a producer and distributor of animal health products based in Malmo, Sweden.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn said this acquisition allows the company to regain ownership of a number of animal health products once owned by the former Pharmacia AB of Sweden. Two of these products are Hylartil, used to treat joint dysfunction in horses, and Hogpax, a tranquilizer for swine.</p>
